 Record design decisions, hypotheses, review findings, and unresolved questions here.
 Imported associated notes retain original evidence/timestamps in `evidence/associated_notes.jsonl`.
+
+## 2026-10-24 repair — guarantee the translated template survives
+
+**Root cause.** Version 2.0.2 grew the color-2 template anywhere on the canvas and validated only color counts. The anchor vector could move some or all template cells outside the grid; the retained default `seed=0, sample_index=0` lost all three translated cells despite the declared in-bounds invariant.
+
+**Repair.** Version 2.1.0 samples anchors and grows the connected template only inside the set of source cells whose translated coordinates are in bounds. `self_check` now verifies palette, unique anchors, template connectivity and every translated coordinate. Exact `blob_size` values 2–6 are honored. The public axis contract was reduced to the three real controls (`grid_h`, `grid_w`, `blob_size`), all endpoints are strict and observable, unknown/non-integer controls and invalid difficulty values are rejected, and `RULE_HASH=72a5479a7579` pins the unchanged canonical authority.
+
+**Evidence.** Eight portable regression tests pass. They include the retained clipping counterexample, a 480-draw default/easy/hard census, exact 2- and 6-cell templates, declared 7×8 and 14×14 endpoints, strict API controls, and protected-Racket checks requiring one cyan output cell per template cell. Repository lint, override contract and defect lint each pass on source SHA-256 `7d87996fa1a1839c588805cd12d2858b7b0d29ed7a0a11c163ce94f88c70a693` (`checks/327c3478236b-lint2`, `checks/327c3478236b-override`, `checks/327c3478236b-defect-lint2`).
+
+**Limits.** This peer repair received focused changed-surface checks rather than a repeated twelve-stage battery. The canonical Racket program was not edited, and integration/acceptance remain owner decisions.
